| **00:00–00:19** | Opens MID-S3E11 cliffhanger: **Evelyn alone fights Khalazar's ~15ft shadow-skinned SKELETAL BAT MOUNT** while rest of allies work at pyramid. She actually casts Protection from Evil and Good, uses **Loran's radiant lance/sword**, each radiant hit disrupts bat's shadow-wings. Bat's scream banishes her celestial elk **Albert/Mr Handsome** back to radiant dimension (not permanently slain), but Evelyn passes CON saves and radiant armour makes magic half-damage save **zero**; bat misses melee attacks under disadvantage. Evelyn ACTUALLY destroys bat skeleton by a critical strike, no assistance by Koh or Krandal. |
| **00:19–00:35** | Inside pyramid, Koh nonlethally psychically downs additional captive elf labourers. Discussed Remove Curse + psychic rescue is **RETRACTED before actual use**; **Krandal does NOT cast Remove Curse on captives**, spell slots retained (GM explicitly says prior deducted slots refunded). Ten minotaurs including Chad Brad carry stable people; **EIGHT minotaurs, two captives each, ACTUALLY go through FIRST completed Darmah Edstream teleportation circle** from hard floor in lower workshop to **Guild basement**. **Buck Wildfire, Alexandre Withers, Phelan/Faelan and other named craftspeople/cook** physically among first evacuated. Edgar Boonfellow carries Phelan and exits as he considers mission complete. **Chad Brad + Corgan Greathorns remain as TWO minotaurs** with heroes. **Darmah + Five Emissaries, Dominic Reeves, Hiroshi and Nopa Ropa** continue or guard second rescue. **NO exact whole rescued headcount can be reconstructed from table's inconsistent 12/16/26/28 mental arithmetic**; claimed planning numbers are not confirmed headcount. Evelyn ACTUALLY resummons THE SAME Albert intact, reassures herself and equips saddle. |
| **00:35–00:50** | Party moves up pyramid, Evelyn **ACTUALLY CUTS BLACK ICHOR FEEDING TUBES to unfinished ~90ft Khalazar-face statue**, black fluid spills from hollow structure; **does not destroy entire statue with this action alone**. Koh sneaks through TWO upstairs side rooms unseen in S3E11: SIX elves in raw-meat provisioning room, freshly butchered hook-horror/grick carcasses and belly pain; EIGHT others in dark water room with crude ~10ft clay/sand/stone seep filter yielding grey drinkable-looking water from black ichor source. He **ACTUALLY nonlethally knocks out all fourteen**. Krandal medical/survival rolls infer workers spent three months with minimal foul food/water sustenance, rather than a voluntary diet; **not proved poison/contagion**. All these workers are positioned for second evacuation but no actual one yet. |
| **00:50–01:00** | Remaining upper bedchamber attendants two captives: **Princess Hissia** and **Keeves**, formerly only suspected. Krandal and Nopa now PHYSICALLY SEE her, and **GM/players positively call her Princess Hissia**. Koh and Dominic attempt quiet nonlethal intervention; **Koh ACTUALLY PSYCHICALLY KNOCKS Hissia UNCONSCIOUS** and Dominic eventually saps **Keeves**, despite briefly suffering psychological grip when he looks upon Khalazar's bed. **Nopa Ropa ACTUALLY receives/carries Hissia down** and Corgan carries Keeves; neither awake or cured at the moment. Second teleportation circle is RETAINED as escape route and to rescue remaining captives, Darmah and supporting groups stand guard downstairs. |
| **01:00–01:09** | Original three heroes each take one of **three recovered organ urns** from Koh **(he now explicitly states they are “in the bag”, confirming S3E11 after-gate custody was recovered, but does NOT retroactively insert unshown bagging scene)**. Approach **IMMOBILE DESICCATED KHALAZAR** in upper purple-bed throne/bedchamber. His **back of skull, chest and rib frame have hollow cavities**, not frontal surgery. Evelyn ACTUALLY rolls/turns body to expose openings; three players ACTUALLY open jars and **PUT organs into back**. The heart beats/grows near body. **First of two stages of true-form rite actually performed**; a separate drop of Koh wrist blood is NOT explicitly placed in tissue on screen. A **time-accelerated SHARED VISION** follows: ancient blue-lit city and boy-tyrant Khalazar/Emperor **Orgoth(el) Argir**; persecution, destroyed shrines, assassinated prior elders, revolting subjects; a red-eyed THREE-EYED man (looks aboleth-linked but ID unverified), a woman faintly resembling Anthela, and long-haired architect **Nym/Narim** separate brain/heart/lungs and put into jars, leaving lifeless body in bed. Centuries later heroes destroy machinery but leave host; time passes until rebirth. Vision GM-presented as ritual revelation, **not independently validated historical document or current surface reality**. |
| **01:09–01:24** | The Delvers find themselves in apparently **fully restored blue/green-lit ancient CITY**, populated by ghostly silhouettes; Khalazar **REGENERATED in a pale long-white-haired muscular elfin form with golden ear cuffs, hook-horror-belt face, bat-wing kilt and flying curved kopesh/spiritual weapon**. At ~300ft range he declares in language heard telepathically “I have returned / you will break.” **Darmah Edstream and Dominic Reeves ACTUALLY APPEAR as inadvertent linked allies in this dream/confrontation because of Koh's active Psychic Whispers network**; Evelyn's elk Albert/Mr Handsome also appears because of their mutual telepathic link. No other Guild/minotaurs automatically pulled inside this scene. Khalazar uses locust magical area effect, radiant bolts, spells akin Shield of Faith and Spiritual Weapon, psychic fear, mummy infection/restraint, teleporting in sand, etc., with some GM-specific spell adjudications. This **city is a shared magical/psychic space revealed to be illusory**, not independently a fully physically rebuilt surface city. |
