| **~02:47–02:49:11.950** | **FINAL CINEMATIC** in Delvers' rebuilt farm tower: old pink ribbon (Scroungy), locket/photo of Anthela and Koh's daughter, half-eaten potato, **WEDDING INVITATION: Evelyn BLACKWOOD (Evelyn Grinkeeper's noble birth name verified S3E03) and Lord ETHAN RENALD/RENAULT TRAVAIL**, signed **“GCT”**, plus **second SEALED RED LETTER from KINGDOM** left unopened. **Invitation actually visible as future wedding proposal/notice; NO WEDDING CEREMONY IS PLAYED**. “GCT” may point to Gentleman Cavalier but expansion and groom relationship require audio/written verification; do not turn a signed invitation into performed marriage. Red letter is hook only, no contents, no mandated sequel. GM explicitly ends entire **Delvers campaign**. Out-of-game says return to The Wastes after break, no playable epilogue beyond this. |

## Confirmed campaign-completion state

**Definitive:** Three organ jars physically reinserted into Khalazar, Khalazar permanently/actually defeated in climactic shared real/dream sequence by **combined three Delvers**, entire ancient pyramid collapses; BOTH rescue teleport circles actually used, surviving main heroes physically return to Guild, MANY captives brought out, Princess Hissia physically awake and reunited, great skeletal bat defeated, all cursed minotaurs finally rest as bones, Noble Hollow cursed land recovers, farm tower rebuilt in ONE-YEAR epilogue. **Do NOT leave previous S3E11 flags “Hissia suspected”, “gate not entered”, “bat alive”, “teleport merely prepared”, “minotaurs ongoing undead” or “Khalazar only future battle” as CURRENT.**

**Unverified/inference only:** All 37 rescued individually (no full list/match); every specific captive cured using Remove Curse (explicitly cancelled); exact blood donation from Koh's wrist (gesture/vision occurs without separately played bleeding action); restored city physical rather than psychic illusion (later collapses to prior throne room); Darmah's exact revival spell after down; Lord Ethan groom identity expansion of GCT and whether actual wedding takes place; unopened red letter's content/foreshadowed continuation; exact fate of minor Guild members not named in final room; all remaining dungeon monsters destroyed. Names of arc-three visionary ancestors and magic descriptions ASR pending.

## Input inventory, method, review queue

Local MCP TWBD repo **initially clean**, branch `main`, HEAD `6cf88c3d6a42c5698ff418cd22fc48ea80ec52f5`. From connected GitHub repo **DEFAULT BRANCH** (not established equal to local HEAD), complete textual exports [P](../../sources/Delvers%20S3E12.%20KOA%20is%20not%20A-OK.parakeet.processed.srt), SHA `9ca7f16780ee9adcb4bcc16c7977b303fe06c8b0` (**2,387 cues, 20,356 Unicode-normalized spoken tokens, ends 02:49:11.950**) and [Q](../../sources/Delvers%20S3E12.%20KOA%20is%20not%20A-OK.qwen-q8.canary-ctc.nemotron.srt), SHA `2595bfc3f312d3a35f6b35ec74a2dbd30c933a29` (**3,977 cues, 20,350 tokens, ends 02:49:11.620**). Complete P read chronologically **0–170 min** in 5-minute buckets (through credits); Q fully parsed for exact text metric, with **selected Q windows** 17–39, 39–60, 60–78, 121–143 and 143–170 min checked, some large outputs truncated. **Q is NOT independently fully read as continuous narrative**. Local workspace first **nine lines of each SRT visually match GitHub remote beginnings**, but **full byte identity is NOT verified**; this analysis is based on identified GitHub default-branch blobs, with local SRT files inventoried. **NO MP3/audio listening, original battle maps, character sheets, clip timing verification or physical lore handouts**. Do not claim audio-verified speech or D&D rules correctness.

Whole-export word distance uses cue chronological content without numbers/times/(speaker N), lowercase, strip apostrophes, Unicode letters+digits tokenize, unit Levenshtein **1,946 / 20,356 = 9.56% INTER-ASR TEXT DISAGREEMENT**, NOT WER. ±3,800 word-index band two-row DP: optimum 1,946 < band proves global exact. [Report](../../reports/DELVERS_S3E12_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md).

**Arc boundaries:** S1E12 Season One FIRST story arc end; S2E12 Season Two SECOND story arc end; **THIS S3E12 concludes SEASON THREE, THIRD STORY ARC, AND ENTIRE PLAYED DELVERS CAMPAIGN (owner-confirmed)**. No S3E13 or mandatory fourth arc. Other **out-of-game** Q&A/bonuses may remain separate, never narrative sequel by default. Campaign source index [Delvers](../README.md).

**Audio/owner review priorities:** last visionary family names “Orgoth(el) Argir”, Shaolin Nym/Narim, three-eyed predecessor, Anthela-like ancestor; when/reason first captive headcount and whether every missing elf physically seen; wording of psycho-vision vs actual body fight; condition of Darmah when she appears in Guild; exact name “Ethan Renald/Renault Travail”, “GCT” signature and implied Gentleman Cavalier identity; date/meaning of unopened red royal letter; exact spell use vs GM rulings. **Next bounded MAIN DELVERS source: NONE, campaign FINISHED; remaining work is listening/editorial verification and any separately identified non-played bonuses**, not S3E13.

